# Code owners for bulwark.
#
# GitHub requests a review from the listed owner(s) on any pull request that
# touches a matching path. The LAST matching pattern wins. A repository ruleset
# / branch protection rule ("Require review from Code Owners") is what turns
# these entries into a hard gate; this file declares the intent.
#
# The whole tree defaults to the maintainer; the security-sensitive surfaces are
# listed explicitly so a future added collaborator still cannot land a change to
# the trust engine, admission gate, scan-source parsers, release/CI plumbing, or
# dependency manifests without maintainer review.

*                           @ranklancer

# --- Supply-chain trust surfaces -------------------------------------------
/internal/verify/           @ranklancer
/internal/admit/            @ranklancer
/internal/cve/              @ranklancer
/internal/registry/         @ranklancer
/internal/updater/          @ranklancer
/internal/reconcile/        @ranklancer
/cmd/bulwark/               @ranklancer

# --- Build, release & CI/CD plumbing ---------------------------------------
/.github/                   @ranklancer
/Dockerfile                 @ranklancer
/Makefile                   @ranklancer
/.goreleaser.yaml           @ranklancer

# --- Security policy & scanning config -------------------------------------
/SECURITY.md                @ranklancer
/.gitleaks.toml             @ranklancer
/.gitleaksignore            @ranklancer
/.pre-commit-config.yaml    @ranklancer

# --- Dependency manifests ---------------------------------------------------
/go.mod                     @ranklancer
/go.sum                     @ranklancer
/web/package.json           @ranklancer
/web/package-lock.json      @ranklancer
